      "description": "Egyptian, Old Kingdom, Dynasty 4, reign of Khufu, ca. 2585–2550 BCE\n\nFrom Abydos, excavations of Flinders Petrie, 1903\n\nH.: 7.5 cm; w.: 2.5 cm; Depth: 2.9 cm\n\nIvory\n\nThe statuette of King Cheops was found in Abydos in 1903. The name of Horus, with whom this great monarch was identified appears on the right side of the throne. When the statuette was excavated, three weeks elapsed between the discovery of the head and the body.\n\nEgyptian Museum, Cairo, JE 36143\n\nCreated with Polycam and iPhone 15 by Peter Der Manuelian, February 15, 2024\n\nThis model should be used for non-commercial, study purposes only"
