      "description": "This statuette portrays King Khufu, famously known as Cheops among the Greeks, renowned as the mastermind behind the construction of the Great Pyramid of Giza. Surprisingly, this diminutive 7.5-cm-tall statue stands as the sole authenticated contemporary three-dimensional representation of this revered king. \n\nUpon its initial discovery at Abydos, the statuette was found with its head missing. Recognizing the significance of the find, Sir Flinders Petrie, in chrge of the excavation, discerning that the break was recent, promptly initiated a search for the missing head, which ultimately culminated in its retrieval three weeks later.\n\nOld Kingdom, 4th Dynasty, reign of Khufu (c.2589–2566 BC) / Abydos / Ivory"
